 {"id": "REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001", "title": "[P1] Fleet-wide: 352 rows on ~28 boards carry off-vocabulary statuses (227 of them \"duplicate\") \u2014 enforce the vocabulary at the writer and canonicalize once", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "type": "task", "created_at": "2026-09-22T15:13:38", "created_by": "review-programme", "description": "Fleet project review #15 (my-project) surfaced this by chasing a single validator error. A mechanical scan of every .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl on the host gives: duplicate 227, parked 56, done 23, open 16, closed 12, completed 8, todo 3, retired 1, resolved 1 = 352 rows across ~28 boards. Top holders: consensus 102 duplicate, hermes4friends-infra 56 parked + 3 duplicate, hermes-dagger 16 duplicate + 7 done, hivemind-work 15 duplicate + 1 closed, musterflow 14, escalation-doctrine 11, ring-runner 9, inference-estimator 7, mafia-ai-benchmark 7, totalstack 6, ring/dashboard/asce/dexdat* 3-5 each, and singles on my-project (resolved 1 + open 2), hermes-canopy (duplicate 1), speclang, uhlp, wojons-mythos, helix, eduos.dexdat.com.co. Root cause: a dedup/cleanup pass wrote \"duplicate\" as a STATUS instead of a canonical status plus a marker field, and nothing re-validated the boards afterwards. Consequences: validator errors on several boards (my-project 1, hermes-canopy 1 of 5, part of bunker's 33); any consumer counting open work by status either counts 227 rows as open forever or drops them; and the same pass can silently re-break a clean board later. boardctl already prints the fix (\"canonicalize with boardctl update <ID> --status ...\"), so this needs a writer-side rule (reject/flag off-vocabulary values at write time, or provide boardctl dup <ID> --of <ID> to write the marker field) plus one sweep.", "acceptance_criteria": "Validator errors attributable to off-vocabulary statuses reach zero fleet-wide; the dedup path writes a marker field (dup_of / superseded_by) rather than a status; a regression test proves an off-vocabulary status is refused or flagged at write time; the sweep is re-runnable and reports per-board before/after counts.", "source": "review #15 my-project \u2014 fleet review programme 2026-09-22", "worker_summary": "Status vocabulary enforced end-to-end: DedupeBackfill merged rows now carry superseded_by=<kept id>; CLI+library regression tests prove update/create --status duplicate|parked|resolved|retired (+aliases) exit 1 writing nothing; new boardctl sweep-status subcommand (dry-run default, --apply canonicalizes alias rows via NormalizeTask only, unknown statuses reported with explicit-decision action, before/after counts). Worker 3 commits (d3ec79f, 82e4349, e4ef77d) merged a028f2f, pushed, gates green, judge PASS.", "foreman_note": "Verdict: .gitreins/history/2026-09-24/325a6ba9/verdict.json (printed id ddfd317b \u2014 printed-vs-disk divergence again). Judge PASS first run; push-before-complete order held. Worktree ~/worktrees/boardctl-REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001 @ wt/REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001 (base 99a56a6), merged + reaped. Session 20260924_051453_20c342.", "worktree": "~/worktrees/boardctl-REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001", "branch": "wt/REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "a028f2f", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "completed_at": "2026-09-24 05:38:00", "sessions": ["20260924_051453_20c342"]}
