a the tool and not direct\".\n\nSEEN IN: coding-hermes review programme, item 70 (heading duplicate ids) and the canopy board regression found 2026-09-23.","detail":{"fingerprint":"18320577634d8432ef35f704d5292b98c0d76cc3982eb7d8220984a59b215491"},"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T01:11:10.037105+00:00","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"6a3981e","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Flock-guarded board writes (worker 6a3981e, merged 9a99f11): advisory flock lock (unix+windows, crash-released) serializes concurrent writers; create id-refusal holds under parallel same-id creates; 394-line stress test demonstrates the interleave race without the lock and green with it; byte-preservation and BT-68 note-append tests intact; README writer note added.","foreman_note":"Wave tick boardctl-2026-09-27-23-52-37; judge PASS verdict .gitreins/history/2026-09-28/cd403865 (printed id 2f3b6de3 is not the dir). Fix direction (c) was already landed (BT-056/067 canon) and not redone.","completed_at":"2026-09-28T01:11:10Z","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-BT-050","branch":"wt/BT-050","sessions":["20260927_191143_14e364"]}
 {"id":"BT-051","title":"Cut v0.1.8: published v0.1.7 predates DF-8/DF-9/BT-048 (drift class reopened on schedule)","status":"complete","priority":"P1","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-23T06:57:16.27479+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"PROVEN LIVE 2026-09-23 (tick 91): downloaded v0.1.7 asset boardctl_linux_amd64 sha256-OK (SHA256SUMS), go version -m -> vcs.revision=f17253b == v0.1.7^{commit}, vcs.modified=false; origin/main is 16 commits ahead carrying 3 user-facing fixes: d4a2c1b DF-BOARDCTL-8 burndown per-day labels (20/20 points vs 2/20), daf0f3f DF-BOARDCTL-9 --skip-bad-lines degrade-with-evidence + validate --repair (9 fleet boards unreadable), 53a79cc BT-048 priority-vocab warnings. README pins v0.1.7 so every documented install path ships stale binaries; RELEASE-2026-09-23-01/-02 block on this cut. Off-by-one answer 2068 (go-cli-release-published-binary-drift) covers the recipe. AC: (1) README Current-release pin + every /releases/download URL moved to v0.1.8; (2) tag v0.1.8 pushed from origin/main tip, CI Multi-Arch release job publishes the 7 platform assets + SHA256SUMS; (3) downloaded v0.1.8 asset sha256-verified, version prints v0.1.8, go version -m vcs.revision == tag commit == origin/main, vcs.modified=false; (4) behavior probe proves >=1 shipped fix vs the v0.1.7 asset (e.g. a DF-9 --skip-bad-lines probe on a bad-line board); (5) CI green on the release push.","detail":{"fingerprint":"44c7b7b33476c046d55ae946ae2c065d9767e6dd5cf999452c691e2e4ea0f501"},"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T07:09:26.939676+00:00","capability_tags":["go","release"],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"a3328d7","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"v0.1.8 cut via the CI tag-push path: README pins moved (0 v0.1.7 hits, 14 v0.1.8), tag v0.1.8 = a3328d7 = origin/main tip; 8 assets incl. SHA256SUMS; downloaded asset sha256-verified, vcs.revision=a3328d7, vcs.modified=false, version v0.1.8; probe: v0.1.8 stats --skip-bad-lines degrades with S