 {"id":"BT-052","title":"Multi-arch releases: verify BOTH triggers publish the full platform set, pin the reusable workflow ref (currently a floating @main), and make Makefile/CI platform-list drift impossible","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-23T07:12:38.208586+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"PREMISE CHECK (2026-09-23) — this is NOT a green-field row.\nThe multi-arch pipeline already exists and is documented. Measured:\n`.github/workflows/multiarch.yml` calls the org reusable workflow\n`coding-hermes/.github/.github/workflows/go-multiarch.yml`, triggers on push\nto main AND on `v*` tags, passes an explicit 7-platform input\n[\"linux/amd64\",\"linux/arm64\",\"linux/arm\",\"darwin/amd64\",\"darwin/arm64\",\n\"windows/amd64\",\"freebsd/amd64\"], and holds contents:write for the release\njob. README.md documents the curl + SHA256SUMS download path and\n`go install`, and **v0.1.8 is published**. So \"add multi-arch builds\" is\nalready satisfied — this row hardens three specific soft spots instead of\nrebuilding something that works.\n\nSOFT SPOT 1 — the reusable workflow is referenced at `@main`, a FLOATING ref.\nAn upstream change to coding-hermes/.github can change what boardctl\npublishes with no commit in this repo — precisely the silent-release-change\nclass that the asset-name parity comment in the workflow already tries to\nprevent. Pin it to a tag or a SHA and record the pin beside the platform\nlist.\n\nSOFT SPOT 2 — the platform list is duplicated in two places (the Makefile\n`release` target and the `platforms:` input) and the only thing keeping them\nequal is a comment saying \"keep these two lists identical\". A comment is not\na check. Add a test that reads both and fails on drift.\n\nSOFT SPOT 3 — prove, do not assume, that BOTH triggers publish: a push to\nmain AND a `v*` tag. The tag ref is what makes the release job run; the\nbranch push must still produce the build. Capture one release run's asset\nlist (7 platforms + SHA256SUMS) as evidence and confirm the README's asset\nnames match byte-for-byte (`boardctl_${goos}_${goarch}`).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- the reusable workflow ref is a tag or a SHA (not @main) and the workflow\n  still runs green on a push to main and on a tag\n- a hermetic check (Go test or a CI step) FAILS when the Makefile platform\n  list and the `platforms:` input diverge\n- the published asset set for the current release is captured as evidence\n  and matches README's names (7 platforms + SHA256SUMS)\n- the pin changes no release CONTENT beyond the ref itself; if moving the pin\n  changes the build, that is a FINDING to report, never a silent fix","detail":{"fingerprint":"22e5a33e4501bf2ab7b5aa82bddc55f63f74bde0197fa7db140c7d30db4a1069"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T12:05:54.00124+00:00","capability_tags":["+infra","+release"],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"57ec269","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Wave worker glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm: multiarch.yml uses: pinned to 917f3216 (full 40-hex main SHA of coding-hermes/.github; upstream has no release tags), pin comment dated beside the platforms input; new internal/workflowcheck (zero deps, 9 tests) fails on Makefile PLATFORMS vs workflow platforms drift/reorder/duplicate and on a floating ref (live RED proof); both triggers proven by run evidence (main-push 35988430750, tag v0.1.8 run 35829487898 with 7 assets + SHA256SUMS). Merged 854b7e7, judge PASS.","foreman_note":"wave tick boardctl-2026-09-24-10-58-10; judge verdict .gitreins/history/2026-09-24/d3512b4c/verdict.json","completed_at":"2026-09-24 07:04:40","sessions":["20260924_060952_3ecd5b"],"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-BT-052","branch":"wt/BT-052"}
 {"id":"BT-053","title":"Roll the board-lint pre-commit hook out to EVERY fleet repo including PAUSED projects, and file the install row in each project's own board","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-23T07:12:38.218814+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"WHY THIS ROW EXISTS\nAn installed hook protects one repo. The fleet has 96 repos under /home/kara\nwith a .git dir, 71 of which already carry the GitReins pre-commit hook. The\noperator's instruction (2026-09-23) is explicit: put the task in ALL other\nprojects INCLUDING PAUSED ones, so the work happens by itself rather than\nbeing retried by hand — \"this way you don't need to try it, they will\".\n\nDEPENDS ON BT-051. Do not start before `boardctl install` exists: the thing\nrolled out must be the TESTED installer, not a hand-copied shell snippet, or\nevery repo ends up with a slightly different hook — the exact drift this row\nis meant to prevent.\n\nDELIVERABLE\n1. A fleet rollout command (a `--fleet <glob|list>` mode of `boardctl\n   install`, or a thin script looping the per-repo installer) that:\n   - enumerates the code repos (with and WITHOUT a board — the installer's\n     own skip path is part of what must be tested)\n   - installs idempotently, CHAINS an existing hook, never clobbers, and\n     prints a per-repo outcome line (installed / already present /\n     skipped-no-board / skipped-no-binary / FAILED + why)\n   - is safe to re-run and safe to run while ticks are live\n2. A row filed in EVERY planet's board naming this rollout, so coverage is\n   visible where the work happens — INCLUDING the PAUSED projects\n   (temple-runner, rabbit-hole, ring-runner, asce, musterflow,\n   escalation-doctrine, Kobayashi-Maru and the paused h3 family). Paused\n   foremen will never run, so the SCRIPT is what installs and the ROW is what\n   records: both halves are required.\n3. A re-runnable census proving coverage: N repos scanned, N hook present,\n   N chained-with-gitreins, N skipped and WHY, plus a list of any repo that\n   could not be installed with its reason. This census is the row's evidence.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- every repo in the census is either installed (hook present AND chained) or\n  skipped with a named, correct reason — no silent misses\n- a repo carrying the GitReins hook still has it afterwards, and BOTH hooks\n  still fire\n- PAUSED projects appear in both the census and the filed rows\n- a SECOND rollout run reports \"already present\" for every repo and changes\n  nothing (idempotence proven, not asserted)\n- the census output is pasted into the row as evidence\n\nSEQUENCING: BT-051 -> this row. Do not run this in the same wave as BT-051;\nthe installer must be merged and released first.","detail":{"fingerprint":"dfc2f6c9453e42e57aafda95a88bc3bd72c6808e0ae814a0f9398e988e003b1f"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T07:12:38.218814+00:00","capability_tags":["+infra","+dx"],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":["BT-054"]}
