eted_at":"2026-09-25T17:26:33+00:00","sessions":["boardctl-2026-09-25-20-33-52"],"depends_on":[],"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/boardctl-BT-060","branch":"wt/BT-060"}
 {"id":"BT-061","title":"[P2] SCOPE: coding-hermes-boardctl — decide what connecting over the muster protocol means for this service","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T15:16:47.782659+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"CONTEXT — what \"connect over muster\" means here (read before scoping).\n\nmuster (github.com/wojons/muster) turns any OpenAPI 3.x spec into a typed CLI\n(openapi-cli), an MCP server (openapi-mcp), a daemon, and a Go library. A consumer\nattaches with one config block:\n\n  {\"mcpServers\": {\"<name>\": {\"command\": \"openapi-mcp\",\n                             \"args\": [\"--spec\", \"<url-or-path>\", \"--base-url\", \"<api>\"]}}}\n\n(muster README \"mcpServers\" + docs/integration-guide.md §2; verified 2026-09-24.)\n\nDESIGN AUTHORITY for every protocol row: muster/specs/PROTOCOLS.md — \"no protocol\nimplementation row may start before its adapter satisfies this spec's pipeline and\ncross-cutting contracts on paper\". The pipeline is discover/ingest -> protocol-neutral\noperation model -> SHARED command+MCP generation -> per-protocol transport executor.\nOpenAPI 3.x is the FIRST adapter, not the engine. muster's board carries PROTO-001..008.\n\n\"Support for people to connect to us over the muster protocol\" therefore means, for this\nproject: (1) publish a muster-consumable OpenAPI 3.x contract for our own service,\n(2) ship the consumer config + a human quickstart, (3) PROVE muster's own binaries\ningest it and drive the live service. Nothing here re-implements muster — we consume it.\n\n             THIS ROW IS ONE THIRD OF A CHAIN (scope -> spec -> build) filed together\n2026-09-24 at the operator's request. Do not start this row until its predecessor\nhas landed; the spec row must not invent a surface the scope row has not decided, and\nthe build row must not guess a contract the spec row has not frozen.\n\n             MEASURED STATE OF CODING-HERMES-BOARDCTL TODAY (2026-09-24, read from the live tree):\n\n             boardctl has an HTTP serve mode but publishes NO contract — measured 2026-09-24: `boardctl serve\n[-C dir] [--addr 127.0.0.1:8787]` exists in the CLI verb list, and grepping cmd/ and internal/ for\nopenapi/OpenAPI returns nothing. So the surface a muster consumer would attach to exists, but its\ncontract is undocumented and unpublished. This repo has unusually strong existing machinery to\nbuild on, and the scope should reuse it rather than invent: internal/describe/registry.go is the\nONE source of --help, `describe --json` and docs/reference.md, cmd/gendocs/ generates the reference\nfrom that registry (\"never hand-written\"), and there is already a route/endpoint parity test\ndiscipline in this repo. A spec generated from the serve route table is the shape that matches.\nBoard rows are the foreman's exclusive responsibility in this fleet (workers must not mutate them),\nso the MCP-safety boundary is not hypothetical here — it is the repo's own standing rule.\n\n             Specific scope questions: (a) which serve routes are GET-only projections (list/show/render/validate)\nversus mutations, and are mutations exposed to a muster consumer at all? This repo's standing rule\nis that board writes are the foreman's alone, so the default must be read-only and the row must say\nso explicitly rather than leaving it to the generator. (b) spec location: generated and committed as\na file, or served live from the route table? Name the parity check either way (this repo already\nfails its build on docs/routes drift — reuse that shape). (c) does `serve` need to answer the\nspec route so a consumer can point --spec straight at the running daemon, and what does that imply\nfor loopback-only binding?\nNOTE: this project also owns the fleet-wide board tooling — if a shared muster config or spec\ngenerator emerges from any of these four chains, boardctl is the natural home for it, and the scope\nrow should say whether it should generalise.\n\n             DELIVERABLE — a written scope, on this row (no code):\n             1. the surface we expose and why that surface (and, explicitly, what we do NOT expose)\n             2. the exact muster consumer block (the mcpServers entry with its real --spec path/URL\n                and --base-url) written out verbatim\n             3. the acceptance test for the later rows: the precise commands a verifier runs, and\n                the assertions that make them non-vacuous\n             4. the boundary call: which operations are agent-safe through MCP and which must be\n                gated (muster's MCP safety contract — mutating operations an agent should not\n                reach unattended)\n             5. the auth story: this service's credential/header vs what muster's config can carry\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: the row closes with the five items above present and concrete enough\n             that the spec row needs no new decision. If a real decision is still open, say so\n             and name who rules on it.","detail":{"fingerprint":"4477c3b94450238dc3da9e16e388bb912e3251cc0d960fa06a613b0e30316a3a"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T21:53:49.069856+00:00","capability_tags":["+integration","+protocol","+interop"],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"44fe805","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Scope doc docs/muster-protocol-scope.md landed in 44fe805 (worker d8fd31a, 469 lines): read-only muster surface (listBoards/getUploaderForm/getOpenapiSpec on a SERVED /openapi.json), POST + board writes explicitly excluded (foreman-only rule standing), verbatim mcpServers block (--spec http://127.0.0.1:8787/openapi.json), non-vacuous acceptance battery A.1-A.8, MCP safety boundary per muster PROTOCOLS.md 4.5 + fleet foreman-only rule + serve non-goals, auth story (loopback-only hard gate, serve.go:94). Full gate green on merged tree; Tier1 guard PASS on worktree commit.","foreman_note":"Decisions D1-D6 landed: D1 read-only surface; D2 served spec (parity = new check-only Go test, BT-062 owns); D3 consumer block verbatim; D4 agent-safe = GET-only, mutating ops gated by exclusion-at-spec; D5 auth = loopback-only, unauthenticated by design; D6 generator generalizes ONLY if a second fleet chain adopts muster (open, ruled at BT-062 review). Worker corrected 3 stale premises in the row reasoning (describe/registry.go + cmd/gendocs do NOT exist at 5737be9; route-parity gate is a pattern, not a build step) — corrections verified by foreman against the live tree. Judge FAIL 2687f62a was board-closeout ordering only (tick-88 class): work judged before row close; re-judge after this update.","completed_at":"2026-09-25T16:53:49+00:00","sessions":["boardctl-2026-09-25-20-33-52"],"depends_on":[],"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/boardctl-BT-061","branch":"wt/BT-061"}
