his repo's rule is\nthat the registry is the single source (see internal/describe and cmd/gendocs). A hand-written spec\nhere would be the exception to that rule and needs its reason recorded. Also: the spec must describe\nthe serve surface as it exists, not an aspirational one; if a route the consumer wants does not\nexist yet, that is a separate row, not a spec fiction.\n\n             DELIVERABLE — the contract and the wiring, frozen on this row:\n             1. the OpenAPI 3.x document muster will be pointed at (file or served route), with its\n                location named precisely and its generation rule stated (hand-written vs generated\n                from the route table — this repo's own doctrine decides which)\n             2. operationIds, request/response schemas, and the servers[] url that muster dereferences\n                (muster falls back to the spec's own servers[].url when --base-url is omitted; a\n                RELATIVE servers url cannot be dereferenced standalone — say which case applies)\n             3. the consumer config block + a three-line human quickstart (the CLI form:\n                openapi-cli <generated-verb>), both added to this repo's docs\n             4. the parity rule: what keeps the spec from drifting off the real routes, in the\n                same shape as this repo's existing drift checks\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: the spec parses in muster's own parser, the consumer block is copy-pasteable,\n             and the parity rule is expressed as an executable check (not a comment).","detail":{"fingerprint":"68b0a4fdbd88df23c0fdeae8c6dd532fa6a16c31ba539a675c04acca4717e295"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T15:16:47.792197+00:00","capability_tags":["+integration","+protocol","+interop"],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":["BT-061"],"worktree":null,"branch":null}
