 {"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-12","title":"P2 — README quickstart's `sha256sum -c --ignore-missing` fails verbatim on a bare download (asset must keep its release filename)","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T18:50:00+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"OBSERVED 2026-09-24 (dogfood run 15, fresh Debian 13 bunker agent 2909fec1). The README install block downloads the binary as boardctl_linux_amd64 and runs sha256sum -c --ignore-missing — that works. But any user who saves the binary under a different name (curl -o bc, browser default name) hits 'sha256sum: SHA256SUMS: no file was verified' and no line names the cause; the README DOES explain the filename requirement in prose three paragraphs later ('The downloaded binary must keep its release filename'), but the failure gives no pointer back to it. Reproduced on the bunker: binary saved as bc, checksum step fails; renamed to boardctl_linux_amd64, passes. WHY IT MATTERS: the checksum step is the trust anchor of the zero-dep install path and its failure mode looks like a corrupt download, pushing users to skip verification. FIX DIRECTION: the SKIPPED-LINES-style evidence pattern the tool already uses — when sha256sum exits with 'no file was verified' the docs (or a tiny wrapper note under the install block) should quote the error and its cause side by side. Docs-only fix.","detail":{"fingerprint":"dg15-df-boardctl-12-checksum-filename"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T23:11:46+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"9ad1e35","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Wave worker glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm: README quickstart recipe PROVEN LIVE against real v0.1.8 assets (curl+sha256sum -c --ignore-missing exit 0, ./boardctl version v0.1.8; 7 published assets listed) — recipe correct as written, no defect; pinned by TestDF12QuickstartBlockPinned (block shape, tag agreement via versioncheck.DownloadURLRe, asset-naming rule, retired spellings banned), live-gated TestDF12QuickstartSHA256SUMSPublishesBinaryAsset (BOARDCTL_DF12_LIVE=1, verified PASS live, skips hermetic), anti-vacuity detector test; versioncheck exported DownloadURLRe for reuse. Merged 639fff8, judge PASS (65e6bfd8).","foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":[],"worktree":"~/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-12","branch":"wt/DF-BOARDCTL-12"}
