-{"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-16","type":null,"status":"pending","priority":"P1","title":"offline make release stamps binaries with a FOREIGN repo's SHA on hosts where the build path is nested under another git repo \u2014 no stamp verification exists in the cut path","reasoning":"Dogfood run 16 (release-path replay) 2026-09-27, worktree build of a3a1dea: make release VERSION=v0.1.9 completed rc=0 in 69s and produced 7 assets whose SHA256SUMS verify clean, but go version -m dist/boardctl_linux_amd64 reports vcs.revision=c6af73f1b4da97a112e634be98285598961fed26 (NOT a boardctl commit - it is the HEAD of /home/kara/.git, an unrelated HOME-level git repo) and vcs.modified=true, while boardctl version prints v0.1.8 (from the tag). Reproduced 3x: worktree build, repeat build, and a build in an OLDER sibling worktree (worktrees/boardctl-BT-RELEASE-0902) all stamp c6af73f+dirty; a main-checkout build stamps the correct a3a1dea. Mechanism (proven against go1.26.6 toolchain source cmd/go/internal/vcs/vcs.go): vcsGit.RootNames matches only a .git DIRECTORY; a linked worktree's .git FILE does not stop FromDir's parent walk, which runs to / when srcRoot is empty; the first .git DIR found above the build path is /home/kara/.git, and gitStatus then reports that repo's log -1 (c6af73f) and 3346 dirty files. On this box EVERY worktree Go build mis-stamps; yesterday (09-26 16:30) the same worktree stamped the correct boardctl SHA, so the trigger is the home repo's HEAD moving to c6af73f at 11:20 today. A releaser following README 'Cutting a release' step 4 (make release offline) ships assets whose provenance metadata is FALSE while sha256 and version-string checks all pass; the only probe that catches it is the repo's own make install-check (verified: FAILs module version, vcs.modified, and DEGRADEDs the ancestry arm - exit 2). FIX DIRECTION: add a stamp assertion to the release target (after the build loop, require go version -m on the linux-amd64 asset to report vcs.revision as a non-empty ancestor of VERSION and vcs.modified=false, else fail loudly naming the foreign SHA), and one docs line under Development: build releases from a checkout whose ancestor path contains no other .git directory (or from CI, which provably stamps clean - v0.1.8 asset verified vcs.revision=a3328d7, modified=false).","detail":{"fingerprint":"ffb19c920541991c91d5e1a2db14a13960b93cea6d6af3489ad0d2808ca04257"},"created_at":"2026-09-27T22:49:06Z","created_by":null,"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"capability_tags":["go","make","release"],"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-27T22:49:06Z"}
-{"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-17","type":null,"status":"pending","priority":"P2","title":"version-check gate validates internal README agreement only \u2014 a release can be cut with stale install URLs pointing at the previous tag","reasoning":"Dogfood run 16, releaser-seat replay of README 'Cutting a release' step 1: internal/versioncheck/versioncheck.go has no input for the tag being cut (Check verifies pin line vs URL tags agree with EACH OTHER), so the documented sequencing 'move surfaces then run make version-check' is enforced only by discipline: skip the README edit, run make version-check (green, 0.23s), tag v0.1.9, push \u2014 CI cuts the release and every /releases/download/ URL in the README fetches the PREVIOUS release. Drift IS caught after the fact (verified: reverting one URL to v0.1.8 FAILs the gate with a precise message naming URL 1 vs the pin line and the fix), but nothing ties the README to the candidate tag BEFORE the cut. Two-part fix direction: (a) extend Check with an optional -expected-tag flag/env (make version-check VERSION_TAG=vX.Y.Z fails while any surface still names an older tag), wired into the README step of the release procedure; (b) one sentence in the Cutting-a-release section stating the gate checks agreement, not currency.","detail":{"fingerprint":"38ca5cec386bab8a7a7d9c0007b0a493e429d78e175bfd5d6a4fbad2e9e3dd11"},"created_at":"2026-09-27T22:50:01Z","created_by":null,"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"capability_tags":["go","make","release"],"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-27T22:50:01Z"}
-{"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-18","type":null,"status":"pending","priority":"P2","title":"sha256sum --ignore-missing exits 0 when zero files matched ('no file was verified') \u2014 gate is sound only because of the exact-name pre-check","reasoning":"Dogfood run 16: coreutils sha256sum -c --ignore-missing prints 'SHA256SUMS: no file was verified' and exits 0 when NOTHING matched (reproduced in scratch: wrong-named binary + SHA256SUMS, exit 0). make install happens to be safe only because Makefile line ~132 pre-checks that the exact released asset name exists in dist/ before the checksum runs (verified: wrong-named file in DIST = loud exit 2, nothing installed). So the checksum gate's soundness hangs on an unnamed ordering invariant: reorder the two checks (or port the gate) and the zero-match hole ships. Calibrates DF-BOARDCTL-12 (filed run 15 as a docs-only finding): the message gap is real but the end-to-end refusal held at HEAD. Fix direction: in the install target, treat 'no file was verified' as failure (count OK lines or require at least one match), and note the ordering dependency in the install target comment.","detail":{"fingerprint":"056a66f6186784f54588a7f3b609e8c35c64da4cbf8d28fae1e18854a09d2925"},"created_at":"2026-09-27T22:50:01Z","created_by":null,"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"capability_tags":["make","release"],"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-27T22:50:01Z"}
